### 6.4 Soll-API (additiv, analyze-route unangetastet)

Neuer Endpoint, nur EOD Close:

```
GET /api/ohlcv?tickers=MSFT,NVO,SPY&from=2024-09-09&to=2026-09-09
```

Antwort:

```json
{
  "from": "2024-09-09",
  "to": "2026-09-09",
  "source": "fmp",
  "bars": {
    "MSFT": [{ "date": "2024-09-09", "close": 408.12 }, "..."],
    "NVO":  [{ "date": "2024-09-09", "close": 138.40 }, "..."],
    "SPY":  [{ "date": "2024-09-09", "close": 547.01 }, "..."]
  },
  "meta": {
    "MSFT": { "n": 504, "first": "2024-09-09", "last": "2026-09-08", "truncated": false },
    "NVO":  { "n": 498, "first": "2024-09-16", "last": "2026-09-08", "truncated": false }
  }
}
```

Regeln:

- max. 12 Ticker pro Request (Portfolio-Größe)
- `to` clamp auf heute (kein Look-ahead)
- `from` clamp auf today−5Y (Starter-Plan)
- leere Serie → `bars[ticker]=[]`, `truncated=true`, keine Interpolation
- Server-Cache Key `ohlcv:{TICKER}:{from}:{to}` TTL **24 h**
- nur `date` + `close` (Kombinationskurs braucht kein OHLC)

from-Datum aus Preset:

\[
from_{6M} = today - 182\,d,\quad
from_{1Y} = today - 365\,d,\quad
from_{2Y} = today - 730\,d
\]

Implementierung Server (~40 Zeilen):

```ts
// server/ohlcv-route.ts  (neu) — mount in routes.ts
app.get("/api/ohlcv", async (req, res) => {
  const tickers = String(req.query.tickers || "").split(",").map(s => s.trim().toUpperCase()).filter(Boolean).slice(0, 12);
  const from = String(req.query.from || "").slice(0, 10);
  const to = String(req.query.to || new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)).slice(0, 10);
  const bars: Record<string, { date: string; close: number }[]> = {};
  for (const t of tickers) {
    const raw = await fmpHistoricalPrices(t, from, to).catch(() => []);
    bars[t] = (Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [])
      .map((r: any) => ({ date: String(r.date).slice(0, 10), close: Number(r.close ?? r.adjClose) }))
      .filter(p => p.date && Number.isFinite(p.close) && p.close > 0)
      .sort((a, b) => a.date.localeCompare(b.date));
  }
  res.json({ from, to, source: "fmp", bars });
});
```

Wenn `bars[t][0].date > from` und Starter-Plan: optional Yahoo-Fallback laut WORK_DATA_PROVIDERS.md §3. Für 1Y/2Y meist unnötig.

### 6.5 Client (PortfolioPage)

Zwei Maps, nicht eine:

```
analysisByTicker.historicalPrices     → Scoring / CAPM-Engine / 52w  (unverändert)
historicalPricesByTickerLong          → Overview-Chart + Attribution-Equity
```

Trigger: `timeframe` oder offene Longs ändern sich.

```ts
const from = timeframeCutoffIso(timeframe); // 6M / 1Y / 2Y
const tickers = [...openLongs, benchmark].join(",");
const res = await apiRequest("GET", `/api/ohlcv?tickers=${tickers}&from=${from}`);
setHistoricalPricesByTickerLong(res.bars);
```

An `PortfolioOverview` **Long-Map** übergeben, nicht den Analyse-Cache.

Kombinationskurs bleibt:

\[
V_t = \sum_i Q_i P_{i,t}^{\text{long}}
\]

Fenster-Rendite:

\[
R_t = V_t / V_{t_0} - 1
\]

UI-Badge wenn `meta.n < sollBars(preset)`:

```
Historie 119 Bars < 252 (1Y) — Chart zeigt verfügbare Spanne, nicht das Label
```

X-Achse = min/max der **tatsächlichen** Long-Serie, nicht der Button-Text „2 Jahre“.

